From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Wed, 1 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fbdev: create the display at 240x240

lv_display_create() initializes the default theme, which picks its size
class (padding, radius) from the horizontal resolution at that moment.
lv_linux_fbdev_set_file() later sets the framebuffer's real resolution
but does not re-pick the class. Creating the display at the panel's
240x240 selects the small class that matches the ST7789V.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/drivers/display/fb/lv_linux_fbdev.c
+++ b/src/drivers/display/fb/lv_linux_fbdev.c
@@ -102,7 +102,7 @@
     LV_ASSERT_MALLOC(dsc);
     if(dsc == NULL) return NULL;
 
-    lv_display_t * disp = lv_display_create(800, 480);
+    lv_display_t * disp = lv_display_create(240, 240);
     if(disp == NULL) {
         lv_free(dsc);
         return NULL;
